<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results - April.</title>
<headline>Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results - April.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan interests bought during April a total of 54,000 tonnes U.S. soybeans, 110,000 tonnes of U.S. corn and 68,000 tonnes U.S. wheat at tenders.</p>
<p>Basic information of April soybean/corn tender results</p>
<p>(Prices based on US$ per tonne)</p>
<p> April Buyer  Tonne  Type Seller     Price   Delivery/Freight</p>
<p>  8    BSPA-T 54,000 soy  Cargill    $.67    May 11-25/CNF</p>
<p> 17    FGEP   54,000 corn Mitsubishi $.7070  July 1-15/CNF</p>
<p> 23    MFIG   31,500 corn Mitsui     $136.70 June 16-30/CNF</p>
<p> 23    MFIG   24,500 corn Mitsui     $.46    June 16-30/CNF</p>
<p>Delivery periods Soybean and corn shipments are slated for the U.S. Gulf Mexico, shipments from the Pacific Northwest are 15 days after the Gulf.  </p>
<p>Basic information of recent wheat tender results:</p>
<p>	 (Prices based on US$ per tonne)</p>
<p>  April Buyer   Tonne  Type  Seller   Price    Delivery/Freight</p>
<p>  23    Flour					    May 5-25/$20.50</p>
<p>	  Mill    17,300 DNS   CGI	$209.03</p>
<p>	  Assoc   11,600 HRW   CGI	$208.29</p>
<p>		     5,100 WW    CGI	$185.64</p>
<p>  23    Flour					    May 20-10/$20.50</p>
<p>	  Mill    18,300 DNS   CGI	$209.03</p>
<p>	  Assoc   11,500 HRW   CGI	$207.91</p>
<p>		     4,200 WW    CGI	$186.21</p>
<p>Wheat tenders comprised Dark Northern Spring (DNS), Hard Red Winter (HRW), White Wheat (WW) and Soft Wheat (SW). Wheat shipments all are slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
